--   **`AxisUA6` from the `A`-line components.**
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.J6SegAxA7`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem J6Seg.Ax.axisUA6_of (P : Prm) (hP : P.Ok) (hStep : AStepNeed6 P) (hKer : AKerNeedA6 P)
--       (tab : Fin 1 → IStmt HS 1) (hFU : FineU6 tab) (hPre : PreA6 P 8 16 17 40 tab) :
--       AxisUA6 P tab
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** `A`-line axis program (`AxisUA6`), part 7: assembly
--
--   **`AKerNeedA6 P`** (the numeric leaf of the `A` axis): eventually, for every axis, kernel
--   parameters satisfying `AKCond` (`J6SegAxA5`; `pk = 8p + 16`, `b = 17p + 40`, input bound
--   `p + 2`, `2^f = 8H`) and the nine non-set-up cost terms of `axACost` (six fine exposures, two
--   slab passes, the kernel run) each `≤ Cb · cU6 P n A / (D + 1)`.
--
--   **`axisUA6_of`**: `AxisUA6 P tab` from `FineU6 tab`, `PreA6 P 8 16 17 40 tab` (B4, the kernel
--   register set-up), `AStepNeed6 P` (A worker, the copy step and the descriptor set-ups) and
--   `AKerNeedA6 P`. The descriptor stack is `dA = 31` (`30` when the fine stack is `31`), the kernel
--   registers `ρK dF` (`10 … 29` without `dF`), the kernel `aKprog2` and the axis body are the
--   machine's own two procedures.
